# These are this reviewer's own substantive judgments after whole material and actual source-table reading.
findings=[
 {'findingId':'CHEMSVA-001','rows':[0],'duties':[0],'title':'BW organic uses are not carried by the two listed property partners','why':'The whole source requires explaining uses in everyday life and technology from properties for the stated organic substances. fcc73fb5 describes/classifies properties and 3d3231f9 explains melting, boiling and solubility through interactions. Neither listed original partner requires the property-to-use explanation. The BW actual target set also lacks the retained petroleum-use atom b95cdf98. Equal atomic sets do not supply this missing operative role.','limit':'This is a bounded source-role coverage hold. It does not assert that all chemistry applications require a new atom or career instruction.','minimalRemedy':'Provide and bind an existing retained goal/operator witness that actually covers the organic property-to-use examples, or retain a narrowly scoped source role until that witness exists.','primaryWitness':{'document':'BP2016BW_ALLG_GYM_CH_V2.pdf','pdfPages':[17],'printedPages':[15],'section':'3.2.1.1 (12)'}},
 {'findingId':'CHEMSVA-002','rows':[1],'duties':[0,1,2,3],'title':'BW experiment planning, actual conduct and protocol duties remain unbound','why':'3.2.1.1(1) requires experimental investigation, whereas fcc73fb5 only describes/orders properties. 3.2.2.1(2) expressly requires plan, conduct, protocol and contextual interpretation; bcf8b24b and the combustion-family children chiefly interpret reactions, air and extinguishing. 3.2.2.2(2) requires actual mass-conservation/mass-ratio experiments and guided evaluation; 1bdaf7f2 evaluates/explains and e0d05c36 recognizes/describes ratios. The separation partner 5a709938 does carry separating and justified procedure choice, but its actual independent planning witness is not bound. These are separate operators, not a numerical-data or safety substitute.','limit':'No actual human experiment is required to assert a candidate; an assessable AI-authored procedural route and exact physical partner duties must exist. This review does not claim any experiment was performed.','minimalRemedy':'Preserve a scoped plan/conduct/protocol route and bind the precise retained practical/operator partners; inspect its whole task and moderator protocol rather than only target IDs.','primaryWitness':{'document':'BP2016BW_ALLG_GYM_CH_V2.pdf','pdfPages':[15,21,23],'printedPages':[13,19,21],'sections':['3.2.1.1 (1),(4)','3.2.2.1 (2)','3.2.2.2 (2)']}},
 {'findingId':'CHEMSVA-003','rows':[4],'duties':[0],'title':'HH societal-development/knowledge links are not equivalent to decision appraisal','why':'The source explicitly asks for links between societal developments and chemical knowledge. 1df17884 requires criterion-led opportunities/risks and decision reflection. Its full DE/EN text does not require explaining the historical or developmental relation between knowledge and society. The second argumentation duty can be exercised by justified criterion-led appraisal, but this does not cover the first duty.','limit':'Only this opaque role is held; no new defect is asserted for the accepted decision goal itself.','minimalRemedy':'Bind a retained whole knowledge-development/application witness for the exact HH stage, or keep this source component pending.','primaryWitness':{'document':'chemie-gym-seki-data.pdf','pdfPages':[20],'printedPages':[20],'section':'3.1 Erkenntnisgewinnung, end-of-SekI column'}},
 {'findingId':'CHEMSVA-004','rows':[6],'duties':[0],'title':'HH elevated polarimetry has no retained operative partner','why':'The actual elevated-only protein table requires the general polarimetry principle. 3d3231f9,747c5777,eb7537dd concern intermolecular forces, electrostatic bond/molecular polarity and properties. Plane-polarized light rotation/optical activity is not molecular dipole polarity. The separate canonical f4d5a02d does have a suitable polarimetry description, but it is absent from this actual candidate target set and absent from the original duty partner list. Chromatography/Rf coverage by 978a6f25 is preserved.','limit':'No polarimetry experiment or quantitative rotation calculation is made universal; the stated source only needs the general principle here.','minimalRemedy':'Bind the existing suitable polarimetry goal into the actual elevated HH source/view scope, preserving original history and the narrower duty.','primaryWitness':{'document':'chemie-gyo-2022-data.pdf','pdfPages':[26],'printedPages':[26],'section':'1.3 elevated-only Analysenverfahren'}},
 {'findingId':'CHEMSVA-005','rows':[10],'duties':[0],'title':'MV metallic-current source role is not established by ionic-lattice partners','why':'The actual compulsory content distinguishes a driving voltage source, moving electrons and vibrating metal ions. The listed original partners 4285d84a,950c73c6,a1632ea9 concern ions in solutions, ionic lattices and ion formation. A metal is not an ionic crystal with mobile ions. The actual retained fcaf8c9b metal-model goal is useful counterevidence and must not be erased, but this duty currently has no exact binding or operative witness for its voltage/electron/vibration mechanism. Its mere target presence cannot certify the full original role.','limit':'This is a targeted source-binding hold, not a claim that the retained metal-model goal is scientifically wrong or that no retained goal could remedy it.','minimalRemedy':'Bind a scientifically correct retained metallic-current model witness for voltage, electron motion and lattice vibration to this exact original duty. No image generation is indicated.','primaryWitness':{'document':'Chemie_Sekundarstufe_I_2021.pdf','pdfPages':[20],'printedPages':[16],'section':'Warum fließt Strom durch Kabel? Verbindliche Inhalte'}},
 {'findingId':'CHEMSVA-006','rows':[12],'duties':[0],'title':'MV elevated conductometric/potentiometric analysis lacks actual method coverage','why':'The actual LK column requires conductometric titration and potentiometry and specifies learner experiments. 02634fdd plans/conducts an indicator acid-base titration; 28c90c6a interprets titration data; the remaining partners cover acid-base/electrochemical theory. Indicator titration or analysis of supplied curves does not itself require performing conductivity/potentiometric measurement. The other listed chromatographic/electrophoretic/spectroscopic description duty has usable retained descriptive partners.','limit':'The hold concerns the two named elevated methods, not all titrations and not an invented real laboratory execution claim.','minimalRemedy':'Bind the exact measurement-device/procedure/recording route and its actual practical partner for these LK methods; preserve indicator-titration validity as a separate role.','primaryWitness':{'document':'Chemie_Gymnasium_11_12_Erprobungsfassung.pdf','pdfPages':[34],'printedPages':[30],'section':'zusätzlich für den Leistungskurs, Elektrochemische Analyseverfahren'}},
 {'findingId':'CHEMSVA-007','rows':[15],'duties':[0,2,4,7],'title':'RP society removal bundles distinct classification, data acquisition and carbon inquiry roles','why':'TF8 requires deriving criteria, collecting and evaluating data about RP chemical industry, but the listed partner 1df17884 covers decision appraisal without collecting/evaluating this industrial data. TF11 requires experiments and data/source use; its c0f1bf09 partner describes cycles rather than conducting inquiry. TF1 classification has a potentially suitable already-retained 02dc29ae goal, but the exact original decision only binds criterion-led societal appraisal and this opaque family, so a corrected specific source binding is still needed. TF11 radiation/greenhouse terms must not be supplied by unrelated visible-dye absorption goals. Other plastics/mobile-energy appraisal components have real retained operator coverage.','limit':'These are bounded original duties and exact scope-bindings. The source extraction merges concept and term columns, so the original raw combined text is preserved and inspected in the actual PDF.','minimalRemedy':'Retain the outstanding collection/inquiry roles and bind the genuine classification/data/practical/climate partners to their exact TF source duties; preserve the valid appraisal components.','primaryWitness':{'document':'Chemie_Sekundarstufe_I_Biologie_Physik_Chemie_2014.pdf','pdfPages':[68,82,88],'printedPages':[66,80,86],'sections':['TF1','TF8','TF11']}},
 {'findingId':'CHEMSVA-008','rows':[16],'duties':[0],'title':'RP carbon inquiry needs experiments and data/source work','why':'The whole TF11 duty combines experiments, data evaluation and use of other sources. Its retained listed partners are 1df17884,542822de,c0f1bf09; the first evaluates decisions, the last describes cycles, and 542822de is itself being removed. None supplies the whole physical inquiry/data/source combination.','limit':'A finite synthetic dataset can support evaluation; it cannot establish that the experimental/source operator is already carried.','minimalRemedy':'Bind an actual finite carbon-inquiry/data/source candidate and the retained procedural partner, with no real learner/human execution claim.','primaryWitness':{'document':'Chemie_Sekundarstufe_I_Biologie_Physik_Chemie_2014.pdf','pdfPages':[88],'printedPages':[86],'section':'TF11 Kompetenzen, first bullet'}},
 {'findingId':'CHEMSVA-009','rows':[17],'duties':[0,1,9],'title':'RP selected photometry and compulsory complex applications are not carried by the listed retained atoms','why':'The actual W1.5 table contains photometer structure/function, extinction and concentration from a calibration graph; its LK additum is Lambert-Beer. 466bd2e9 only assigns IR/1H-NMR basic signals; the dye partners cover electronic color and absorption spectra, not quantitative photometry. Independently, actual P9.1 explicitly requires applications of complex formation at at least two selected examples; redox/polymer/catalysis/silver partners do not carry a named coordination-complex application route. This compulsory gap suffices independently of optional photometry. The extraction wrongly reports overview pages for detailed content and flattens optional extensions into source atoms.','limit':'W1.5/W9.2/W17.2 are conditional selections, not universal LK obligations; environmental analysis uses alternative water OR soil paths. The page36 IR/NMR/GC-MS etc extensions and page73 extensions are not made universal. The hold does not require both alternative environmental paths or every extension.','minimalRemedy':'Restore the real P/W/extension/page/course frame and bind the exact selected photometry route and the two-example P9.1 complex application witness. Keep other original roles and original decisions unchanged as history.','primaryWitness':{'document':'Chemie_Sekundarstufe_II_MSS_2022.pdf','pdfPages':[19,20,21,35,36,57,58,73],'printedPages':[19,20,21,35,36,57,58,73],'sections':['1.5 W','9.1 P LK','9.2 W LK','17.2 W alternatives']}},
 {'findingId':'CHEMSVA-010','rows':[18],'duties':[1],'title':'RP compulsory climate/acidification content needs an explicit retained witness','why':'Actual P17.1 includes natural/anthropogenic greenhouse effect, greenhouse gases, climate change and sea/soil acidification. Listed 1df17884 appraises decisions,580b3616 identifies three gases and c0f1bf09 describes cycles. Their whole bodies do not establish this whole climate/radiation/acidification content. Criterion-led societal relevance and at least one additional cycle have useful retained carriers, but they cannot certify this distinct compulsory content block.','limit':'No universal all-example list is invented; the additional element-cycle examples are alternatives, and this is a source-content witness hold.','minimalRemedy':'Bind an actual retained climate/acidification source-content witness in the exact P17.1 scope, keeping the valid appraisal and cycle roles.','primaryWitness':{'document':'Chemie_Sekundarstufe_II_MSS_2022.pdf','pdfPages':[72],'printedPages':[72],'section':'17.1 P Fundamentum'}},
 {'findingId':'CHEMSVA-011','rows':[19,26,31,34],'duties':[0],'title':'Mandatory secondary-element classification/function is not bound to a retained operative example','why':'RP4.4 P requires one primary, one secondary and one fuel-cell example; SN12LK compulsory left column enumerates primary, secondary and fuel cells; TH common column requires classifying all three and explaining one example each. c8844ac6 explicitly transfers galvanic principles to primary cells and evaluates battery types; f0939f88 explains a galvanic cell and fd7977bf describes forced electrolysis. This does not yet bind the required actual secondary-element classification/recharge/function example. The canonical lead/lithium secondary-cell goals 27e4fe9b and 6b82f80e exist but are absent from these actual target sets. f4fa58e7 is thermodynamics/sustainable-energy/detergent structure, not an assessed secondary-cell example.','limit':'The SN documentation/presentation/digital-media right-column remarks have recommendation status and are not the reason for this mandatory-content hold. RP LK additional examples remain its own actual additum; no human battery experiment is claimed.','minimalRemedy':'Bind a suitable existing secondary-cell goal/example and exact source route, or an assessable whole retained goal witness covering the required classification and charging/discharging function, while keeping primary/fuel roles.','primaryWitness':{'documents':['Chemie_Sekundarstufe_II_MSS_2022.pdf','lehrplan-gymnasium-chemie-sachsen-2025.pdf','LP_GY_Chemie_2024.pdf'],'pdfPages':[[42],[57],[53]],'printedPages':[[42],[45],[48]],'sections':['4.4 P','SN12 LK LB1 left column','TH electrochemical sources common column']}},
 {'findingId':'CHEMSVA-012','rows':[21],'duties':[2,3],'title':'SN mandatory carbonate experiment and selected historical route remain unbound','why':'SN9 LB2 left column explicitly requires experimentally forming/decomposing limestone. The listed criterion-appraisal,reaction-distinction and cycle-description partners do not carry actual formation/decomposition conduct. The chosen WB history-of-brewing role is an insight into historical/social effects, not merely present-day decision appraisal by 1df17884. Carbonate reaction equations/interpretation remain useful but do not replace experiment conduct.','limit':'WB history applies only if that optional learning area is selected. Examples and the right-column remarks are preserved as recommendations; no universal excursion or all named limestone subexperiments are invented.','minimalRemedy':'Bind a actual experiment-conduct witness and the selected historical-insight witness to these exact retained source roles.','primaryWitness':{'document':'lehrplan-gymnasium-chemie-sachsen-2025.pdf','pdfPages':[4,28,30],'printedPages':['IV',16,18],'sections':['Verbindlichkeit/Bemerkungen','SN9 LB2','SN9 WB1']}},
 {'findingId':'CHEMSVA-013','rows':[24],'duties':[3],'title':'SN LK redox titration is not covered by acid-base indicator titration','why':'The compulsory left column at PDF49/printed37 requires actual conduct and quantitative evaluation of redox titrations. 02634fdd specifically requires an acid-base indicator titration. pK/puffer/acid-base-curve goals and redox-equation balancing do not establish an actual redox titration with its electron stoichiometry and endpoint method. The chromatography duties have usable method/Rf partners; they do not close the separate redox titration.','limit':'Manganometry and water testing are right-column examples; they are not both made universal. The compulsory redox-titration conduct/evaluation operator itself remains mandatory.','minimalRemedy':'Bind the proper retained redox-titration procedure/evaluation witness; do not rename a neutralization calculation as a redox experiment.','primaryWitness':{'document':'lehrplan-gymnasium-chemie-sachsen-2025.pdf','pdfPages':[4,49],'printedPages':['IV',37],'section':'SN11 LK LB2 compulsory left column'}},
 {'findingId':'CHEMSVA-014','rows':[29],'duties':[2],'title':'TH common/elevated course metadata wrongly includes elevated-only TLC in GK','why':'The actual TH introduction states that the left column is common to both courses and the right column is additional for elevated level. At PDF57/printed52 the ninhydrin TLC learner experiment is in the right column. The whole sourceGoal 157-03 and normal facet classify it GK_LK, and the neutral GK row consequently treats it as a common source duty. Identical GK/LK candidate target sets do not repair this course error.','limit':'This is a concrete course-binding hold on the GK occurrence. It does not revoke the corresponding LK physical method role or require general-level students to perform elevated-only TLC.','minimalRemedy':'Create a new exact metadata/operative-scope successor that restricts this duty to the elevated course, preserving original historical extraction/decision and common chromatogram/Rf interpretation.','primaryWitness':{'document':'LP_GY_Chemie_2024.pdf','pdfPages':[43,57],'printedPages':[38,52],'sections':['4.1 column definition','4.1.7 right-column TLC experiment']}},
]
